Description: hwmon ABI: drop fanN_min, report EC sentinels as -ENODATA, hide fan4
 fanN_min was always writable (0644), also in read-only mode, without lock
 and without any effect (D6). It is removed (HWMON_F_MIN and the cache).
 .
 A tachometer value of 0xffff was reported as 65535 RPM (D8). It is now
 -ENODATA; 0 stays a valid reading (fan stopped). The temperature
 sentinels 0x00 and 0xff (already -ENODATA upstream) are named constants.
 .
 fan4 (PCIe, DCR5) has no tachometer input; upstream returned a constant
 0 RPM, the same value as a stopped fan, distinguishable only by the label
 (D12). fan4_input and fan4_label are now hidden; pwm4/pwm4_enable stay.
 n5-fangov does not read fan4 (fixed channel table, HasTach=false) and
 the F8b watcher samples fan1-fan3 only.
 .
 Resolves D6, D8, D12 (hidden attribute).
 .
 Tested: build/static analysis as 0001. Not tested on hardware: sysfs
 listing (no fanN_min, no fan4_*), sensors output, n5-fangov start.
Author: SirRenix <7069603+SirRenix@users.noreply.github.com>
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-09
